  "reasoning": "The claim was denied with CO-50 (not deemed medically necessary), which is a substantive denial rather than a coding or administrative error, so resubmitting the same data will not resolve it. The payer does not offer peer-to-peer review or retroactive authorization, leaving a formal appeal as the only viable path to challenge the medical necessity determination. Historical data shows that while success rates are mixed, appeals are the only action with a non-zero probability of recovery compared to write-offs or billing the patient.",
